WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.964 --> 00:04.968 align:center line:79%
I express my love
for President Russell M. Nelson

00:06.670 --> 00:11.909 align:center line:79%
and my gratefulness for the remarkable
influence he has had on each of us

00:13.510 --> 00:15.512 align:center line:81%
and, in all of our names,

00:16.914 --> 00:21.785 align:center line:79%
I thank God for the noble life
of President Dallin H. Oaks.

00:25.622 --> 00:28.725 align:center line:79%
With each passing year,
I feel greater love for our Savior,

00:28.725 --> 00:31.361 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ, and for His
merciful Atonement.

00:32.296 --> 00:34.231 align:center line:81%
His supreme sacrifice,

00:34.231 --> 00:35.732 align:center line:81%
securing victory over death

00:35.732 --> 00:41.104 align:center line:79%
and sin, is the most consequential
contribution of all human history.

00:42.506 --> 00:46.043 align:center line:81%
Understanding His divine gift is, for me,

00:46.043 --> 00:50.113 align:center line:79%
an open-ended heavenly tutorial
that will continue beyond the grave.

00:51.448 --> 00:54.585 align:center line:79%
The powerful compassion
of the Savior in forgiving sin

00:54.585 --> 00:57.721 align:center line:79%
and in healing the wounds
caused by the sins of others,

00:58.989 --> 01:02.459 align:center line:79%
is a most miraculous manifestation
of the love of God.

01:03.727 --> 01:08.265 align:center line:79%
My desire is to offer hope
for those seeking forgiveness

01:08.265 --> 01:10.033 align:center line:81%
for very serious sins,

01:10.934 --> 01:14.705 align:center line:79%
and to offer comfort to those seeking
healing from the anguishing

01:14.705 --> 01:18.241 align:center line:79%
wounds caused by the serious
sins of others.

01:19.409 --> 01:24.014 align:center line:79%
Healing and forgiveness are each
found in their fulness

01:24.014 --> 01:26.183 align:center line:81%
in the atoning love of Jesus Christ.

01:27.684 --> 01:32.189 align:center line:79%
If you have committed serious
sins and are in the process of

01:32.189 --> 01:36.994 align:center line:79%
or have the desire to fully repent and
feel the unspeakable joy of forgiveness,

01:38.328 --> 01:41.198 align:center line:81%
please know this miracle is awaiting you.

01:42.132 --> 01:46.003 align:center line:79%
The Savior continuously
calls, “Come unto me.”

01:47.871 --> 01:49.172 align:center line:81%
Strengthening your faith

01:49.172 --> 01:54.144 align:center line:79%
in our Savior, Jesus Christ,
will invigorate the yearning of your soul

01:54.211 --> 01:58.915 align:center line:79%
to know Him, believe in Him,
and yield your heart to Him.

01:59.916 --> 02:02.352 align:center line:81%
Enos asked about his own forgiveness,

02:02.753 --> 02:04.688 align:center line:81%
“Lord, how is it done?”

02:05.322 --> 02:09.526 align:center line:79%
The Lord responded,
“Because of thy faith in Christ,

02:09.826 --> 02:12.663 align:center line:79%
whom thou hast never
before heard nor seen.”

02:13.463 --> 02:18.568 align:center line:79%
And Moroni added, “If ye shall deny
yourself of all ungodliness,

02:18.568 --> 02:22.706 align:center line:79%
and love God with all
your might, mind and strength,

02:23.106 --> 02:26.343 align:center line:81%
then is his grace sufficient for you.”

02:27.978 --> 02:30.747 align:center line:81%
Turning from sin, turning toward God,

02:31.048 --> 02:34.985 align:center line:79%
and strengthening your faith
in Jesus Christ is a beautiful beginning.

02:36.086 --> 02:41.491 align:center line:79%
Humbly submitting your will to God
includes acknowledging serious sins

02:41.491 --> 02:43.660 align:center line:81%
to your bishop or branch president,

02:44.227 --> 02:48.532 align:center line:79%
but your full forgiveness
comes from the Savior.

02:49.166 --> 02:54.204 align:center line:79%
Forgiveness is a divine gift
offered through the grace of Jesus Christ.

02:55.939 --> 03:02.045 align:center line:79%
A desire to truly return
to God is accompanied by the determination

03:02.412 --> 03:06.616 align:center line:79%
to be completely honest
with your Heavenly Father, with yourself,

03:06.850 --> 03:10.687 align:center line:79%
with those who were harmed,
and with your priesthood leader.

03:12.389 --> 03:16.193 align:center line:79%
Your Heavenly Father rejoices
in your resolve to come unto Him

03:16.493 --> 03:18.929 align:center line:81%
with a broken heart and contrite spirit.

03:19.830 --> 03:24.201 align:center line:79%
Having a contrite spirit is humbly
putting yourself in the hands of God;

03:24.968 --> 03:30.240 align:center line:79%
having a broken heart brings what the
Apostle Paul described as “godly sorrow,”

03:30.674 --> 03:35.712 align:center line:79%
a deep longing of the soul
to return to Him whatever the cost.

03:37.714 --> 03:41.685 align:center line:79%
Your yearning leads you
to want to repair what you have broken.

03:42.586 --> 03:48.391 align:center line:79%
Yet, realizing some things are not
in your power to repair, you

03:48.425 --> 03:52.195 align:center line:79%
fervently pray that the Lord,
through His grace,

03:52.796 --> 03:57.267 align:center line:79%
will help heal those who have been hurt
in consequence of your actions.

03:59.436 --> 04:05.509 align:center line:79%
The effects of serious sin on others are
often painfully difficult to overcome.

04:07.544 --> 04:10.447 align:center line:79%
Are you following the example
of the sons of Mosiah,

04:11.348 --> 04:16.086 align:center line:79%
who were “zealously striving to repair
all the injuries which they had done”?

04:16.987 --> 04:21.091 align:center line:79%
Speak with those you respect
about what you might not be seeing.

04:22.425 --> 04:24.094 align:center line:81%
As I was preparing this talk,

04:24.094 --> 04:28.565 align:center line:79%
I received an unexpected email from
someone in the process of repenting

04:28.865 --> 04:31.168 align:center line:81%
and desiring to return to the Church.

04:32.135 --> 04:36.473 align:center line:79%
His former wife was still suffering from
the loss “of [their] eternal marriage,

04:36.940 --> 04:40.243 align:center line:79%
[difficulties with the children],
the loss of financial security, ...

04:40.243 --> 04:43.213 align:center line:79%
not [being] quite able
to keep up with the expenses,

04:43.647 --> 04:47.150 align:center line:79%
[and] the deeply suffocating feelings
of being betrayed.”

04:48.652 --> 04:52.222 align:center line:79%
He shared with me how his priesthood
leader “felt impressed

04:52.222 --> 04:57.093 align:center line:79%
to [ask him] to prayerfully consider
what [more he could do for his former wife

04:57.093 --> 05:01.298 align:center line:79%
and children].” With permission,
I share a part of his email.

05:02.566 --> 05:04.367 align:center line:81%
“I [first] thought the [money] I gave up

05:04.367 --> 05:07.270 align:center line:79%
in the divorce decree
was more than generous,

05:07.270 --> 05:11.041 align:center line:79%
but my branch president
encouraged me to fast and pray about it.

05:11.641 --> 05:13.810 align:center line:81%
... Initially, I struggled with the idea

05:13.810 --> 05:18.148 align:center line:79%
of further restitution.
Since my sins weren’t financial,

05:18.548 --> 05:21.751 align:center line:79%
I wondered what a ’generous
restitution’ truly meant ...

05:22.185 --> 05:25.589 align:center line:79%
but I soon realized it
wasn’t just about money.

05:26.456 --> 05:30.393 align:center line:79%
My priesthood leaders met
with [my former wife] and my children

05:31.595 --> 05:35.065 align:center line:79%
and realized they were still
struggling and hadn’t healed.”

05:35.866 --> 05:38.935 align:center line:79%
“My new goal was to move
forward with faith. ...

05:39.202 --> 05:44.574 align:center line:79%
I simply expressed my desire
to help with no strings attached. ...

05:45.775 --> 05:49.980 align:center line:79%
I decided to [send my former wife]
a specific amount per paycheck,

05:50.347 --> 05:53.216 align:center line:79%
which was a significant
portion of my net pay.

05:54.317 --> 05:56.820 align:center line:81%
Just before making the first payment,

05:57.187 --> 06:01.258 align:center line:79%
the Lord [impressed upon my mind
that I needed] to pay [twice that amount].

06:02.259 --> 06:05.695 align:center line:79%
I’ve learned that restitution
isn’t just about money.

06:06.229 --> 06:09.499 align:center line:79%
It’s about humbly
dedicating my life to the Lord. ...

06:10.133 --> 06:15.238 align:center line:79%
The money is to help replace what I took
from my family due to my poor choices.

06:15.839 --> 06:20.677 align:center line:79%
It’s about making and keeping promises
without expecting anything in return,

06:21.311 --> 06:27.183 align:center line:79%
and helping her not worry about
bills so she can seek the Spirit.”

06:29.486 --> 06:33.723 align:center line:79%
Your efforts to restore what you have
broken may have nothing to do with money,

06:34.491 --> 06:39.529 align:center line:79%
but as you humbly counsel with the Lord,
you may find there is more you can do.

06:41.631 --> 06:44.000 align:center line:79%
As you seek the Lord’s
forgiveness, be patient

06:44.000 --> 06:46.303 align:center line:81%
as you wait upon His full approval.

06:46.903 --> 06:48.405 align:center line:81%
Consider this scripture:

06:48.972 --> 06:54.177 align:center line:79%
“[They] humbled themselves ... in the
depths of humility; ... and ... did cry

06:54.210 --> 06:56.413 align:center line:79%
mightily to God; yea, even
all the day long ....

06:57.113 --> 07:01.685 align:center line:79%
[But the] Lord was slow to hear
their cry because of their iniquities.”

07:02.619 --> 07:08.892 align:center line:79%
“Nevertheless, the Lord did hear their
cries and ... began to ease their burdens;

07:09.392 --> 07:13.763 align:center line:81%
and ... they began to prosper by degrees.”

07:14.931 --> 07:22.872 align:center line:79%
Be patient as the Lord gives you
His blessing and approval by degrees.”

07:22.872 --> 07:25.976 align:center line:79%
In the Lord’s time,
you will feel His voice telling you,

07:26.509 --> 07:29.279 align:center line:81%
“Let these things trouble you no more.”

07:30.080 --> 07:33.616 align:center line:79%
One day, as you continue
to turn to the Savior,

07:33.984 --> 07:37.387 align:center line:79%
your Heavenly Father
will take “away the guilt from [your]

07:37.654 --> 07:39.556 align:center line:81%
heart, through the merits of his Son.”

07:43.293 --> 07:47.297 align:center line:79%
For you who have been so unfairly
injured by the serious sins of another,

07:47.931 --> 07:52.469 align:center line:79%
I long to share the Savior’s love
and compassion, His comfort and peace.

07:53.336 --> 07:56.272 align:center line:79%
The sadness you have felt,
the heartbreak, the loss,

07:56.539 --> 07:59.142 align:center line:81%
the suffocating feeling of betrayal,

07:59.509 --> 08:02.479 align:center line:79%
the upending of your life
as you imagined it to be—

08:03.146 --> 08:05.482 align:center line:81%
I give you my absolute assurance

08:05.682 --> 08:08.151 align:center line:81%
the Savior knows you and loves you.

08:08.785 --> 08:12.555 align:center line:79%
Reach out to Him.
He is your comfort and strength.

08:13.123 --> 08:15.492 align:center line:81%
He will send His angels to bear you up.

08:16.659 --> 08:19.963 align:center line:79%
When will your pain be gone,
your grief subdued,

08:20.330 --> 08:22.632 align:center line:81%
the unwanted memories forgotten?

08:23.533 --> 08:26.936 align:center line:81%
I do not know. But this I do know.

08:27.737 --> 08:32.742 align:center line:79%
He has the power to bring
beauty from ashes of your suffering.

08:34.244 --> 08:37.814 align:center line:79%
Our beloved brothers and sisters
in Grand Blanc, Michigan,

08:38.415 --> 08:41.017 align:center line:79%
with their undaunted faith
in Jesus Christ,

08:41.017 --> 08:43.086 align:center line:81%
with their courage and unselfishness,

08:43.286 --> 08:46.556 align:center line:79%
have and will in the weeks
and months ahead,

08:47.357 --> 08:52.896 align:center line:79%
abundantly receive of the Savior's
incomparable love and grace.

08:54.631 --> 08:57.534 align:center line:79%
And as you continue
to place your trust in Him,

08:58.735 --> 09:05.041 align:center line:79%
your clouds of darkness and anguish
sobbing in the night will be

09:05.408 --> 09:10.914 align:center line:79%
transferred into cascading tears
of joy and peace in the morning light.

09:11.548 --> 09:16.853 align:center line:79%
“Your sorrow shall be turned into joy ...
and your joy no [one] taketh from you.”

09:17.654 --> 09:19.756 align:center line:81%
That moment will come.

09:20.523 --> 09:23.226 align:center line:81%
I testify that it will come.

09:27.163 --> 09:31.935 align:center line:79%
The atoning love of Jesus Christ can be
found in the most difficult situations,

09:32.335 --> 09:36.106 align:center line:79%
but we all constantly need
the atoning grace of our Savior.

09:36.706 --> 09:41.778 align:center line:79%
President Dallin H. Oaks
taught, “Because of His atoning experience

09:41.778 --> 09:46.216 align:center line:79%
in mortality, our Savior is able
to comfort, heal,

09:46.483 --> 09:49.419 align:center line:79%
and strengthen all men
and women everywhere,

09:50.253 --> 09:56.392 align:center line:79%
but I believe He does so only for those
who seek Him and ask for His help.

09:57.427 --> 09:59.062 align:center line:81%
The Apostle James taught,

09:59.796 --> 10:04.000 align:center line:79%
’Humble yourself in the sight of the Lord,
and he shall lift you up.′

10:04.801 --> 10:09.639 align:center line:79%
We qualify for that blessing
when we believe in Him

10:09.973 --> 10:11.941 align:center line:81%
and pray for His help.”

10:14.777 --> 10:17.046 align:center line:81%
I received permission from my dear friend,

10:17.046 --> 10:22.619 align:center line:79%
an emeritus General Authority, Elder
Robert E. Wells, now 97 years old,

10:22.952 --> 10:26.923 align:center line:79%
to share his experience
of more than 60 years ago.

10:27.857 --> 10:33.763 align:center line:79%
While living in Paraguay in 1960
and employed as an international banker,

10:34.397 --> 10:39.002 align:center line:79%
Robert Wells, then 32 years old,
and his wife, Merle,

10:39.435 --> 10:46.342 align:center line:79%
were each a pilot in two different planes
flying home from Uruguay to Paraguay.

10:47.210 --> 10:49.012 align:center line:81%
Encountering thick clouds,

10:49.479 --> 10:53.249 align:center line:79%
Robert and Merle lost visual
and radio contact with each other.

10:54.050 --> 10:59.088 align:center line:79%
Robert quickly landed, where he learned
his wife’s plane had crashed.

10:59.856 --> 11:05.228 align:center line:79%
Neither his wife nor their two
friends flying with her had survived.

11:05.762 --> 11:12.268 align:center line:79%
His children at home in Asunción
were ages seven, five, and two.

11:13.503 --> 11:15.438 align:center line:81%
Elder Wells spoke of his grief:

11:16.239 --> 11:19.175 align:center line:79%
“Words will forever be
inadequate in expressing the

11:19.175 --> 11:21.110 align:center line:81%
pain that swelled within me,

11:21.611 --> 11:25.081 align:center line:79%
consuming my emotions
and numbing my senses.

11:25.615 --> 11:29.852 align:center line:79%
Profound tears of sorrow
simply wouldn't stop flowing.

11:30.920 --> 11:32.422 align:center line:81%
To make matters worse,

11:32.989 --> 11:37.060 align:center line:79%
as my mind was attempting
to deal with the devastating realization

11:37.060 --> 11:38.561 align:center line:81%
of my wife's passing,

11:39.295 --> 11:43.132 align:center line:79%
I found myself experiencing
tremendous guilt

11:43.466 --> 11:46.469 align:center line:79%
for feeling I was responsible
for the crash.”

11:48.538 --> 11:52.875 align:center line:79%
Robert blamed himself for not having
had the plane inspected more thoroughly,

11:53.343 --> 11:57.013 align:center line:79%
and for not giving his wife
better instrument-flying instructions.

11:57.680 --> 12:00.350 align:center line:81%
He felt he was guilty of neglect.

12:01.351 --> 12:05.355 align:center line:79%
Robert said, “My mind went
into a dark daze. ...

12:05.888 --> 12:09.325 align:center line:79%
I simply existed [for the sake
of the children] nothing more.

12:10.260 --> 12:12.729 align:center line:81%
I ... lost my desire to continue on.”

12:13.930 --> 12:18.801 align:center line:79%
In time, Robert was blessed
with a deeply spiritual experience.

12:19.402 --> 12:26.843 align:center line:79%
He recounted: “One evening, about one
year later, while on my knees in prayer,

12:27.377 --> 12:32.415 align:center line:79%
a miracle occurred. While praying
and pleading to my Heavenly Father,

12:33.082 --> 12:36.219 align:center line:79%
I felt as though the Savior
came to my side,

12:36.886 --> 12:43.393 align:center line:79%
and I heard an audible voice speaking
these words to my soul and to my ears:

12:44.160 --> 12:50.133 align:center line:79%
’Robert, my atoning sacrifice paid
for your sins and your mistakes.

12:50.767 --> 12:52.302 align:center line:81%
Your wife forgives you.

12:52.702 --> 12:54.203 align:center line:81%
Your friends forgive you.

12:54.637 --> 12:56.939 align:center line:81%
I will lift your burden.′

12:58.775 --> 13:03.646 align:center line:79%
From that moment the burden of guilt
[and despair] was amazingly lifted from

13:03.713 --> 13:08.351 align:center line:79%
me. I had been rescued! I immediately
understood the encompassing power

13:08.351 --> 13:12.488 align:center line:79%
of the Savior’s Atonement and
... that it applied directly to me.

13:13.323 --> 13:17.994 align:center line:79%
I ... experienced light and joy
like I had never before known. ...

13:18.628 --> 13:23.299 align:center line:79%
I had been given an unearned gift—
the Lord’s gift of grace. ...

13:23.966 --> 13:27.737 align:center line:79%
I didn’t deserve it—
I had done nothing to merit it,

13:28.271 --> 13:30.807 align:center line:81%
but He gave it to me nonetheless.”

13:32.709 --> 13:38.881 align:center line:79%
Brothers and sisters, may we each “be
sanctified in Christ by the grace of God,

13:39.382 --> 13:42.218 align:center line:79%
through the shedding
of the blood of Christ, ...

13:42.218 --> 13:44.554 align:center line:81%
[becoming] holy, without spot.”

13:45.488 --> 13:51.294 align:center line:79%
I testify of the love, the mercy,
and the grace of our Savior and Redeemer.

13:51.894 --> 13:54.263 align:center line:81%
He lives. We are His.

13:54.731 --> 13:58.601 align:center line:79%
We are children of the covenant.
As we believe in Him,

13:59.102 --> 14:01.637 align:center line:81%
follow Him, and trust Him,

14:02.071 --> 14:05.808 align:center line:79%
He will lift us from
our sorrows and our sins.

14:06.442 --> 14:11.481 align:center line:79%
Then, beyond this mortal life
in our Father’s house,

14:12.181 --> 14:15.785 align:center line:81%
we will live with Him forever and ever.

14:16.285 --> 14:19.021 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

